From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:01:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: keep EEE off at the PHYs

The PPE MACs do not do 802.3az LPI: the driver gives phylink no
lpi_capabilities and has no mac_*_tx_lpi ops. Without those ops phylink
does not touch the PHY's EEE settings at all, so the QCA8075, QCA8081
and RTL8261BE keep advertising EEE from their defaults and negotiate it
with any partner that does too. The link then enters low-power idle
that the MAC knows nothing about.

Qualcomm's own driver does not allow this: qca-ssdk disables EEE on
every port at init (qca_hppe_interface_mode_init() clears
port_eee_cfg.enable and lpi_tx_enable), on IPQ95xx as well. On
IPQ807x, OpenWrt's qca_ppe driver found that egress injected while a
port wakes from LPI can wedge that port's queue manager, and users of
this board report EEE-related latency jitter on the 10G WAN port.

Provide empty mac_enable_tx_lpi/mac_disable_tx_lpi ops. With them and
no lpi_capabilities, phylink_bringup_phy() takes its "MAC wants EEE
always disabled" path and calls phy_disable_eee() before the first
autonegotiation, so no port advertises EEE, and ethtool --set-eee is
refused with -EOPNOTSUPP instead of turning on something the MAC cannot
handle. The ops themselves are never called.

Based on the OpenWrt qualcommax qca_ppe change by Julius Bairaktaris
("qualcommax: qca_ppe: disable EEE to prevent idle-port egress wedge").

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24188
Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
index 1101161eb..5cf61810a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -1124,11 +1124,27 @@ static struct phylink_pcs *ppe_port_mac_select_pcs(struct phylink_config *config
 	return ppe_port->pcs;
 }
 
+/* The PPE MACs are not set up for LPI: no lpi_capabilities are given to
+ * phylink, so these are never called. Providing them makes phylink treat
+ * the MAC as "EEE always off" and disable EEE advertisement at the PHY.
+ */
+static int ppe_port_mac_enable_tx_lpi(struct phylink_config *config,
+				      u32 timer, bool tx_clk_stop)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void ppe_port_mac_disable_tx_lpi(struct phylink_config *config)
+{
+}
+
 static const struct phylink_mac_ops ppe_phylink_ops = {
 	.mac_config = ppe_port_mac_config,
 	.mac_link_up = ppe_port_mac_link_up,
 	.mac_link_down = ppe_port_mac_link_down,
 	.mac_select_pcs = ppe_port_mac_select_pcs,
+	.mac_disable_tx_lpi = ppe_port_mac_disable_tx_lpi,
+	.mac_enable_tx_lpi = ppe_port_mac_enable_tx_lpi,
 };
 
 static const phy_interface_t mac_interfaces[] = {
